{
  "slug": "context-os",
  "name": "Context Os",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "Context OS helps Claude Code find the right files faster. It builds a local repo graph of paths, symbols, imports, line counts, and hot files, then injects a compact autocontext block with up to five likely file candidates for each prompt. It runs locally with no server, no embeddings, and no telemetry. Live proof in the repo shows 40.9 percent aggregate token reduction across 36 Claude Code calls.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **3 skills**, **2 commands** and **2 hooks**.\n\n- **Skills** (3): `doctor` (Validate context-os setup, graph availability, and local hook health in the current repository), `init` (Initialize context-os in the current project by building the local repo graph and installing Claude Code guidance), `stats` (Show current context-os graph status, git state, and recent session signals for the active repository)\n- **Commands** (2): `outline` (Show a file's structural map (symbols + line ranges) so you can read only the slice you need), `savings` (Show your context-os token savings — all-time, this week, streak, and a shareable card)\n- **Hooks** (2): `SessionStart`, `UserPromptSubmit`\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install context-os@claude-community` from `sravan27/context-os`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude"
  ],
  "pluginType": "package",
  "package": {
    "skill": 3,
    "hook": 2,
    "command": 2
  },
  "sourceType": "community",
